From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: require the WAN receive queue for optical learning

The source port in msg1 selects the PON netdev independently of the QDMA
that delivered the descriptor. Require the physical WAN receiver as well
as the published service before the packet can trigger PPE learning.
Keep ordinary data and control delivery unchanged.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1045,2 +1045,3 @@
 static void airoha_qdma_learn_skb(struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev,
+				 struct airoha_qdma *rx_qdma,
 				 struct sk_buff *skb, u32 hash, u32 msg0)
@@ -1055,3 +1056,3 @@
 	/* Only one descriptor supplies provenance for the entire frame. */
-	if (skb_is_nonlinear(skb))
+	if (rx_qdma != &dev->eth->qdma[1] || skb_is_nonlinear(skb))
 		return;
@@ -1204,5 +1205,5 @@
 		reason = FIELD_GET(AIROHA_RXD4_PPE_CPU_REASON, msg1);
 		if (reason == PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED)
-			airoha_qdma_learn_skb(dev, q->skb, hash, msg0);
+			airoha_qdma_learn_skb(dev, q->qdma, q->skb, hash, msg0);
 
 		done++;
